---
// privacy.astro — Archex Ecosystem Privacy Policy
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Archex"
  description="Archex Ecosystem Privacy Policy. Explaining our data handling practices, purpose-specific consent, and privacy rights across archexweb.in."
  canonical="https://www.archexweb.in/privacy/"
  activePath="/privacy"
>
  <div class="shell legal-container">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <span class="tech-tag">Legal & Data Governance</span>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy<span class="hl-dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">
        <span>Effective Date: November 2026</span>
        <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
        <span>Applies to: archexweb.in and related parent brand properties</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Indian Legal Review Advisory Callout -->
    <div class="legal-advisory" role="note">
      <div class="advisory-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
          <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
          <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="advisory-text">
        <strong>Legal Notice & Indian Regulatory Context:</strong>
        This Privacy Policy outlines data handling practices for Archex. While drafted to uphold core data protection principles including the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (India), formal operational policies remain subject to final review and counsel by an Indian legal practitioner.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Operator Identity & Brand Architecture</h2>
        <p>
          This website (<strong>archexweb.in</strong>) is operated by <strong>Archex</strong> as the parent brand and central gateway for the Archex ecosystem.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Archex ecosystem operates through three complementary practices:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Archex Craft</strong> (craft.archexweb.in) — Software engineering and technical product development.</li>
          <li><strong>Archex Studio</strong> (studio.archexweb.in) — Brand identity, UI/UX design, and creative direction.</li>
          <li><strong>Archex GTM</strong> (gtm.archexweb.in) — Go-to-market strategy, positioning, and growth execution.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When you submit an enquiry through this parent website, your communication is processed by Archex and directed to the practice or practices relevant to your initiative.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
          We deliberately minimize the personal data we collect. Information is gathered primarily when you voluntarily provide it through our dedicated enquiry form:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact Details:</strong> Your full name and work email address.</li>
          <li><strong>Project Context:</strong> Company or organization name, practice of interest, description of enquiry, approximate budget range, and timeline expectations.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical Transmission Data:</strong> Standard server logs (e.g., IP address, browser user-agent, timestamp) collected automatically for security, DDoS mitigation, and spam detection.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not collect passwords, sensitive personal data, or payment instrument details through this gateway.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Purpose-Specific Processing & Separation of Consents</h2>
        <p>
          We process your information strictly based on specified, lawful grounds:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Enquiry Processing (Legitimate Intent / Contract Preparation):</strong> When you submit a project enquiry, the data provided is processed solely to assess your requirements, direct your message to the appropriate practice lead, and reply to you. Agreeing to enquiry processing is necessary to receive a response.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Marketing & Insights (Optional Distinct Consent):</strong> We maintain an absolute separation between enquiry handling and marketing communications. You will only receive occasional insights, articles, or announcements if you have explicitly checked the optional marketing consent box. You may withdraw marketing consent at any time without affecting ongoing project communications.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Data Sharing & Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. Information is shared only under strict conditions:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Practice Leads:</strong> With team members within Archex Craft, Archex Studio, or Archex GTM as required to evaluate and respond to your enquiry.</li>
          <li><strong>Infrastructure Providers:</strong> With hosting, cloud compute, and email delivery providers operating under confidentiality and security agreements.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal Obligations:</strong> Where mandated by applicable law, court order, or governmental authority in India or relevant jurisdictions.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Data Retention & Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          We retain enquiry submissions for as long as necessary to facilitate discussions and manage prospective client relationships (typically up to 24 months following initial contact), unless a formal client agreement is established.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may request the deletion or correction of your submitted information at any time by contacting us as described below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Security Measures</h2>
        <p>
          We implement industry-standard technical measures to safeguard information against unauthorized access, loss, or alteration. All web traffic to archexweb.in is enforced over HTTPS with TLS encryption. Administrative access to enquiry records is restricted to authorized personnel.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Your Rights & Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your jurisdiction and under the provisions of the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (India), you have the right to request access to, correction of, or erasure of your personal data held by Archex, as well as the right to withdraw previously granted consent.
        </p>
        <p>
          To exercise any privacy rights or submit questions regarding this policy, please reach out via our dedicated <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/contact">Contact Page</a> specifying your privacy request.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-container {
    padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(60px, 9vw, 110px);
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .hl-dot {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .meta-sep {
    color: var(--line);
  }

  /* Advisory Callout */
  .legal-advisory {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--signal);
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .advisory-icon {
    color: var(--signal);
    margin-top: 2px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .advisory-text {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
  }

  .legal-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 20px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-section li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--signal);
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--signal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>

